From 6fe3bf1ddc855148fa897da09d66fee6ea5b0529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 05:39:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Foresight tray system and polished 2i standalone

Brings two previously uncommitted apps into the repo and fixes several
bugs found by running them.

Foresight UI (foresight/)
- foresight_ui_v17.html: fix the V16 material library, which was appended
  with literal "\n" sequences instead of newlines. CSS reads \n as the
  character 'n', so every selector parsed as `n:root[data-material=...]`
  and matched nothing. All 12 materials (steel, aluminum, brass, bronze,
  copper, gold, cz, opal, four marbles) were dead; verified 0/12 -> 12/12.
- foresight_ui_v18.html + polygon_layer.html: render trays as polygons
  with feathered strokes, and restore the tray show/hide launcher that
  renderMenu() had left as an empty stub. Position and size are left to
  the freeform counter.

Tray design rules (foresight/polygon_shape_library.py)
Encodes the rules as executable constraints: bans squares, rectangles and
regular polygons; requires no two side lengths to match and angles not to
be uniform; keeps triangles wide-based with a bulbous peak; feathers the
perimeter within 0.6-0.8px; supports sharp, rounded and mixed corners.
Silhouettes are seeded per tray, so same-type trays differ visually but
stay stable across reloads.

Content-driven fitting (foresight/tray_requirements.py)
Modules declare the space they need, never the shape they want; any
family that can hold that space qualifies. Measures usable area by
inscribed rectangle rather than bounding box, since chamfers eat into it.
Raises rather than shipping a tray its content overflows.

2i Writer's Room (2i/)
- Fix a crash in loadDocState from an undefined rerenderContinuityFlags,
  which silently broke Open Document, drag-and-drop and Restore Autosave.
- Refresh the editor on load and clear it on New Document, which also
  leaked the previous book's characters and plot threads.
- Stop the manuscript scrolling to the bottom on every selection.
- Make Ctrl shortcuts work with CapsLock on, guard unsaved work on tab
  close, allow Enter to submit modals, and add focus-visible styles.

Tests: 31 passing (23 shape rules, 8 existing polygonal suite).

